### Employment Management System | MySQL
About the Project

This is a MySQL project I built to practise database design and SQL analysis using an employee management scenario.

As a fresher, I wanted to build a project that goes beyond basic SQL queries and gives me experience working with a complete relational database. The project covers employee information, departments, job roles, attendance, payroll, leave, qualifications, and performance.

The main focus was to understand how SQL can be used to organise data, maintain data quality, and answer questions that could be useful to an HR or management team.

Technologies Used
MySQL
SQL
MySQL Workbench
Database Design

I designed the database with 8 related tables:

Employees
Departments
JobRoles
Attendance
LeaveRecords
Payroll
Qualifications
Performance

I used Primary Keys and Foreign Keys to connect the tables and followed normalization principles to keep the database structured and reduce duplicate data.

I also created an Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD) to understand and document the relationships between the tables.

SQL Analysis

I developed 80+ SQL queries to practise analysing employee and HR data.

Some of the areas I worked on include:

Employee information and experience
Department analysis
Job role analysis
Salary and payroll analysis
Attendance analysis
Leave analysis
Employee qualifications
Performance analysis
Top-performing employees

While writing these queries, I focused on understanding what information could be useful to a business rather than only practising SQL syntax.

SQL Views

I created Views to make commonly used information easier to access:

Employee_Details_View
Department_Summary_View
Attendance_Summary_View
Payroll_Summary_View
Performance_Summary_View

This gave me practical experience in creating reusable datasets for reporting and analysis.

Stored Procedures

I created Stored Procedures for common database operations:

GetEmployeeDetails
GetDepartmentEmployees
GetEmployeePayroll
GetTopPerformers
GetDepartmentSalarySummary

This helped me understand how database operations can be made reusable instead of writing the same SQL repeatedly.

User-Defined Functions

I created functions for common employee calculations:

CalculateAge()
CalculateAnnualSalary()
EmployeeExperience()

These functions helped me practise writing reusable SQL logic.

Triggers

I implemented Triggers to practise automatic data validation and maintain data integrity.

trg_ValidateLeaveDates
trg_Payroll_Before_Insert

For example, the leave trigger checks leave dates before the data is stored in the database.

Indexes

I created indexes on frequently searched columns to learn how database indexing can help improve query performance.

Examples:

Employee_Email_IDX
Employee_Department_IDX
Employee_Job_IDX
What I Worked On

Through this project, I gained hands-on practice in:

Designing a relational database
Creating and connecting multiple tables
Writing SQL queries for business analysis
Working with Primary Keys and Foreign Keys
Using JOINs, subqueries, CTEs and aggregate functions
Using Views and Stored Procedures
Creating User-Defined Functions
Working with Triggers
Creating Indexes
Thinking about data from a business perspective
Business Questions

I used SQL to answer questions such as:

Which departments have the most employees?
Which departments have the highest average salary?
Which employees have the highest performance ratings?
How does salary vary across different job roles?
What are the attendance and leave patterns?
Which employees have the most experience?
How much is being spent on payroll?
Which employees are among the top performers?

These questions helped me understand how SQL analysis can support HR reporting and decision-making.

Key Achievements
Built a complete 8-table MySQL relational database as an individual project.
Developed 80+ SQL queries to analyse employee and HR data.
Practised turning business questions into SQL queries and useful results.
Created Views, Stored Procedures and Functions to make database operations reusable.
Implemented Triggers to practise data validation and data integrity.
Used Indexes to understand basic database performance optimization.
Designed an ERD to plan and document the database structure.
Learning Outcome

This project gave me practical experience with MySQL and helped me build confidence in writing SQL for data analysis.

As a fresher, one of my main goals with this project was to understand not only how to write SQL, but also how to use data to answer a business question.

I will continue improving this project as I learn more about data analytics, database development, and data engineering.
